WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.620
Welcome to Grade 1 English, Unit 1: Welcome to School.

2
00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:07.660
You will learn the words for things
in your classroom, some colour words,

3
00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:10.700
and how to say your own name and how old you are.

4
00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:15.840
School is a happy, welcoming place, and
this unit helps you feel at home in it.

5
00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:22.340
Say the words out loud and enjoy them — this is about
brave first steps in English, not perfect spelling.

6
00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:28.320
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

7
00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:35.380
By the end of this unit, you will be able to name
common classroom objects (table, chair, book, pencil…)

8
00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:39.280
You will also name and point to
colours (red, blue, green, yellow…)

9
00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:41.600
You will also say “My name is ___.

10
00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:43.500
I am ___ years old.

11
00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:44.180
I like ___.”

12
00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:47.460
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

13
00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:54.360
Your vocabulary work begins with these
words: cat, bat, hat, mat, map, can.

14
00:00:55.440 --> 00:01:00.020
Listen to each word, look at what it means,
and try to use it when you talk and write.

15
00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:05.540
The reading sequence includes Amal's
First Day and Talk about Welcome to School.

16
00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:11.600
Read slowly, look at the pictures,
and find the big idea in each text.

17
00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:15.740
When you answer a question, point to the words that show it.

18
00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:20.700
The first language focus is Name a thing in your classroom.

19
00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:24.260
Hold up one classroom object and name it.

20
00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:30.080
Say 'a' before most words, but 'an'
before a vowel sound: a pen, an apple.

21
00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:33.760
Look at the examples, then try
the pattern in your own sentences.

22
00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:38.200
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1 - Listen and point.

23
00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:41.260
Say your ideas clearly and listen to your partner.

24
00:01:41.780 --> 00:01:47.720
In writing, you will draw, trace, copy or write,
then check your work with a grown-up or the AI tutor.

25
00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:49.580
You are ready to begin.

26
00:01:50.180 --> 00:01:55.740
Start with the words, then the reading and the
questions, then the grammar, speaking and writing.

27
00:01:56.280 --> 00:02:02.080
Ask the AI tutor for help any time, and bring your
questions to a live session too if you join one.
